module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.binding_chosen_by_pool_membership_rather_than_by_the_declared_rule

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data binding_chosen_by_pool_membership_rather_than_by_the_declared_rule: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "binding_chosen_by_pool_membership_rather_than_by_the_declared_rule" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**binding chosen by pool membership rather than by the declared resolution rule** (THE ROOT IN ONE SENTENCE, AND IT IS AN ASYMMETRY: A COPRODUCT ARM IS POOL-VISIBLE CORPUS-WIDE WHILE NOT BEING A LOCAL BINDING UNDER ITS OWN SPELLING. ",

    "An off-chain module that imports nothing may reference another module's arm name and receive only an ADVISORY -- unlisted import use -- never a refusal; and INSIDE the declaring module not even that advisory fires, because there the spelling is in source_visible_names. ",

    "That is why the specimen was silent. ",

    "INVALID STATE: two modules declare one spelling -- one as a top-level type, one as an arm of a coproduct -- and a reference to that spelling binds to whichever declaration the assembled pool happens to contain, with no diagnostic at the referencing site. ",

    "THE INVARIANT THIS FALSIFIES, NAMED, because 'the verdict depends on scope' understates it -- IRRELEVANT-SCOPE EXTENSION INVARIANCE: for source S with resolved dependency closure C, an environment E1 derived from C and an environment E2 that is E1 plus declarations UNREACHABLE from S, typecheck(S, E1) must equal typecheck(S, E2). ",

    "It does not. ",

    "The local judgement consumes more environment than its subject owns, which is the defect in one line and is what a repair has to restore rather than merely make the specimen green. ",

    "HARM: the same source is ACCEPTED under one closure and REFUSED under another, and the refusal names an innocent site in a module that neither declares nor imports the competing type. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT, and it is what separates this from an ordinary ambiguity: THE VERDICT FLIPS ON THE PRESENCE OF AN UNRELATED, UNIMPORTED MODULE, so closure composition -- not the source -- decides the type. ",

    "SPECIMEN AND DISCRIMINATING RED, both entry-scoped and therefore reachable on the ordinary acceptance path: gunbc.floor_cost_distribution declares RightCensoredCost as an arm of ClaimCostReading while v2.workflow.claim_cost_observation declares a same-named standalone product, and the first module does not import the second; a 21-module closure over the first alone compiles with 0 blocking errors, while a 45-module closure that adds only the second reproduces the required-floor refusal character for character -- if branches resolve to incompatible types: Coproduct(ClaimCostReading) vs Product(RightCensoredCost). ",

    "The isolating synthetic is three modules and a 6-module closure: A declares Shape = Circle or Square and returns one variant per if-arm; B declares an unrelated Square; C imports A and B. ",

    "A never imports B, C need not import B's Square at all, and the verdict flips on B's mere presence -- symmetric under swapping which arm collides. ",

    "THAT SYNTHETIC IS COMMITTED RATHER THAN DESCRIBED, because a row citing a probe that no longer exists is a transcription wearing a citation's clothes -- the numbers survive and the thing that produced them does not, so the row rots the moment anyone doubts it. ",

    "It lives in fixtures.if_join_pool_binding as four modules: declaring_module holds the subject and is byte-identical across both arms, colliding_module is the whole of the perturbation, and closure_with_collision and closure_without_collision are the two entry points. ",

    "The merge-path consumer of those four files is test.claim.if_join_pool_binding_witness_test, admitted on required_gate_prefixes in THIS PR: it folds tools.multi_module_compile_fixture over two manifests that differ only in colliding_module membership, and both arms now expect compile-clean because the product-channel repair lands in the same tree. A v1-compiler-tests cargo-test module was added here and deleted: cargo test is compiled by clippy and run by nobody (gunbc.rung_drop rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path). gunbc#10740 authored the same consumer with the collided arm pinned RED as a defect; this PR supersedes that enrollment by landing the inverted (both-clean) witness with the repair, which is the option review 61772 named. Isolated off-chain PRODUCT collision is what the four-file fixture isolates. type_name_declares_own_type (widening) consumes v1.compiler.infer_env lookup_binding_on_chain: an imported product is on-chain and is not widened to a pool coproduct arm of the same spelling; an unimported pool product is not. The presence-census gate remains str_bindings-only. Reproduce the isolated product pair with gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root fixtures/if_join_pool_binding --entry fixtures/if_join_pool_binding/closure_with_collision.dag against the same command at closure_without_collision.dag -- both entries compile clean after this repair; a revert of the widening carve-out reds the collided entry. THIS DOES NOT CLOSE THE CLASS. The production specimen that remains red under this same repair is Primitive(Observed) vs Coproduct(BeltObserve) at gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate, re-derived by running this binary on the gunbc#10683 tree as gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-dir dag/gunbc/roadmap. This repair does not unblock that production specimen. An isolated unit-arm analogue of the four-file geometry (Dummy import, collider present, declaring_module unchanged) does not reproduce that production diagnostic under this repair, so this row does not record unit-arm as fixed; remaining-channel isolation from the production pair is a separate lane. ",

    "THAT FIXTURE NOW HAS AN EXECUTING CONSUMER, which it did not when it landed: for its first weeks nothing in the tree named the directory -- no Rust test, no gate, no witness row -- so the class had a ratified rule, a committed synthetic and a next-rung trigger with NOTHING THAT COULD GO RED, which is the tier DESIGN section 4b rates worse than an absent check because a committed fixture is read as coverage. test.claim.if_join_pool_binding_witness_test reads those four files and hands them to tools.multi_module_compile_fixture as two manifests -- with and without colliding_module, the SAME declaring_module bytes in both -- and is admitted at exact module grain by v2.workflow.required_floor required_gate_prefixes, so the two arms fold on the required floor of every push. ",

    "ITS COLLIDED ARM WAS PINNED RED AS A DEFECT, NOT AS A CONTRACT, while the compiler still refused: gunbc#10740 enrolled that. THIS PR LANDED THE PRODUCT-CHANNEL REPAIR AND REWROTE THAT ARM -- both manifests now expect compile-clean, which is DESIGN section 4b(4)'s expecting-red probe flipping to a permanent regression control, not the witness breaking. A revert of the widening carve-out reds the collided arm again. ",

    "THE DISCRIMINATION WAS DEMONSTRATED BY MUTATION rather than assumed, on the pre-repair witness: deleting colliding_module from the perturbed manifest redded the collided arm and left the positive control green, and pointing any manifest path at a file that does not exist refuses the read rather than rendering as zero diagnostics. After the repair both arms stay green under that same membership perturbation; the read-miss control is unchanged. ",

    "The fixture is deliberately OUTSIDE the compiled source roots: an authentic collision committed into dag or src/v2 would be a real corpus fork, so the specimen is source handed to the compiler by a fixture, which is the position DESIGN section 4b names when it asks whether a RED is authorable. ",

    "SO THE RED WAS AUTHORABLE ON THE ENTRY-SCOPED PATH AND NEEDED NO WHOLE-CORPUS HARNESS, which is the DESIGN section 4b question asked before the check. The product-channel probe is now a regression control: both fixtures compile clean; a revert of the widening carve-out reds the collided entry. Remaining channels of the class are not permanently green. ",

    "MECHANISM, stated because the obvious reading is wrong: resolution is LOCAL-FIRST -- v1.compiler.infer_env lookup_binding_by_name tries the module's own bindings, then its ancestry bindings, then the intern table, and only on a miss reaches global_bare_lookup -- so a local declaration is not being outranked. ",

    "A coproduct ARM is simply not a local binding under its own spelling, so the arm reference misses local lookup entirely and lands in the pool beside the foreign top-level type. ",

    "Downstream, v1.compiler.infer lookup_variant_parent_enum and variant_owner_node widen a record literal to its owner coproduct only when the binding does not declare its own type on-chain. Before this repair an unimported pool product made type_name_declares_own_type true via global_bare, so the collided arm stayed bare; after it, only str_bindings and ancestry_str_bindings count, so the declaring module's arm still widens. ",

    "THE RULE THIS SUBSTRATE ALREADY HAS, AND THE REASON THIS IS NOT A CALL FOR A NEW ONE: namespace-resolution-design.md section 13, operator-ratified 2026-07-21, is ANCESTOR-CHAIN UNIQUENESS -- exactly one on-chain candidate resolves, two-plus on-chain refuses as a typed AmbiguousReference, zero on-chain refuses as UnresolvedType -- and its host bracket NAME_RESOLUTION_POLICY_NAMESPACE_ONLY defaults to TRUE. ",

    "That rule is LIVE on the function-signature channel, where a cli_run test must explicitly set the policy false to assert first-hit-wins and then re-asserts that the default REFUSES the two-parent homonym. ",

    "IT IS LIVE ON THE TYPE CHANNEL TOO, AND THAT IS THE FINDING -- THE RULE IS NOT BYPASSED, IT IS ASKED ABOUT AN INCOMPLETE POPULATION. ",

    "THIS ROW ASSERTED THE OPPOSITE FIRST, and the retraction is kept rather than overwritten because the wrong version is the one a reader will re-derive: behavior alone said the policy was not running, and behavior alone was wrong twice about this class. ",

    "THE DISCRIMINATING PAIR, entry-scoped, isolating exactly ONE variable -- same policy, same chain geometry, same closure size. ",

    "TWO SAME-NAMED TOP-LEVEL TYPES both on the referencing module's chain REFUSE correctly, with the right message and the right population: ambiguous reference 'Zorkle': 2 candidates, naming both declaring modules and telling the author to qualify, alias or rename. ",

    "CHANGE ONE CANDIDATE FROM A TOP-LEVEL TYPE TO A COPRODUCT ARM, holding everything else fixed, and there is NO AmbiguousReference at all: the foreign product binds silently and the refusal surfaces later as the branch-join mismatch. ",

    "A third-module variant of that arm gives the same result and removes the last confound, that the reference sat inside its own declaring module. ",

    "So the wall is alive and the arm is simply not in front of it. ",

    "THE MECHANISM IS LOCATED IN THE SOURCE AND IT IS A DELIBERATE RULE WITH A STATED RATIONALE, not an omission: v1.compiler.infer_env global_bare_fallback_invariant declares that global_bare tracking is decl-only over type, fn and data names PLUS ONLY THOSE Disj VARIANT ALIASES THAT ARE UNIQUE ACROSS THE WHOLE BARE-NAME SPACE -- a variant whose name any type, fn or data declaration claims stays qualified-only and NEVER BECOMES A GLOBAL_BARE CANDIDATE -- because admitting it would create a type-versus-variant tie that refuses every FAR use of the type. ",

    "SO THE REPAIR IS NOT TO COMPLETE THE POPULATION, and that proposal is withdrawn: re-admitting arms re-creates exactly the tie the exclusion exists to prevent. ",

    "What the exclusion actually does is trade one refusal for another and take the SILENT one -- it protects far uses of the type at the cost of the arm's OWN declaring module and chain losing their arm without a diagnostic, which is DESIGN section 5's rule that a failure arm must refuse rather than widen, applied to a tie that is suppressed globally instead of reported locally. ",

    "The decidable question the repair has to answer is therefore WHERE THE TIE IS REPORTED, not whether the arm is a candidate; and the exclusion's own justification is about FAR uses, which is the asymmetry a locality-respecting rule would exploit. ",

    "A SECOND ROUTE TO THE SAME HARM IS DELIBERATELY NOT FOLDED IN HERE, because folding it in would hide it: when the referencing module IMPORTS both competing modules, the competitors arrive through ancestry_str_bindings, a MAP with one entry per name, so the bind is settled by whichever import won at map-build time and global_bare_lookup is never consulted at all. ",

    "THAT IS WHAT THE TWO-COMPETING-TOP-LEVEL-DECLARATIONS-WITH-IMPORTS PROBE MEASURES, and it is recorded because the next reader will run it and misread it: it silently picks and reds on the picked declaration's shape, and that is evidence about the map grain, NOT about the policy branch, which is what it was first taken for. ",

    "The longest-common-prefix tiebreak global_bare_nearest_ancestor is reached ONLY on the non-namespace-only arm and is therefore DEAD CODE under the shipped default, so deleting it is parallel-authority hygiene and CENSUSES NOTHING -- recorded because a census over unreachable code returns the empty set for the same reason a healthy tree does, and the two are indistinguishable in the output. ",

    "It sits beside a measurement hook -- record_global_bare_ambiguous_silent_pick -- that already NAMES the behavior a silent pick in the source. ",

    "THE HOOK IS NOT MERELY INERT, IT IS INERT IN TWO SEPARATE WAYS, and both were read rather than assumed. ",

    "FIRST, the SILENT-PICK-GATE in the gunbc binary CONSULTED only the fn_parent_first_hits field of the telemetry and exited 1 on it; the global_bare_lcp_picks and global_bare_lcp_ties vectors -- the type and value channel, which is this class -- were COLLECTED AND NEVER READ. Past tense throughout, because THAT GATE NO LONGER EXISTS: it was deleted as permanently green, and the disposition and its reasons are recorded further down this row. The observation is kept because it is what made the gate worth examining at all, and a reader who meets only the deletion cannot tell what was wrong with the thing deleted -- but in the present tense it describes a mechanism nobody can find. ",

    "SECOND, resolution_silent_pick_enable is reached only after the --source-root arm has already exited, so on every modern compile the telemetry is never armed at all and the gate guards only the legacy --source-dir flat scan. ",

    "The deficit was observed, named in the source, given a recorder and a gate, and the gate does not cover it -- SO THE GATE CANNOT GO RED ON THIS CLASS BY CONSTRUCTION, and has not been able to since the --source-root path landed -- permanently green for TWO INDEPENDENT REASONS, wrong field and wrong code path, either of which alone would suffice. ",

    "That is worse than an absent check and DESIGN section 4b says why: it will be CITED AS COVERAGE, because a reader who finds a fail-closed exit 1 on silent picks concludes the class is walled. ",

    "THE TWO REASONS ABOVE ARE CORRECTED HERE RATHER THAN OVERWRITTEN, because the wrong version is the one a later reader would otherwise re-derive, and because one of them would have sent the repair in a direction that could not work. THE SECOND REASON IS FALSE FOR THE LIVE GATE: v1_compiler.cli_run compile_emission -- the transaction every --source-root compile reaches -- DID arm the telemetry through a SilentPickSession and DID carry a Refused arm with phase silent-pick-gate. Only the copy in v1_compiler.bin.gunbc main sits below that transaction's process exit, and that copy guarded the legacy --source-dir flat scan nothing in the repository passes. ",

    "THE REAL REASON IS ONE NEITHER OF THEM NAMED, AND IT IS SINGLE AND STRUCTURAL: EVERY PRODUCER OF ALL THREE CHANNELS SITS BEHIND THE DEAD ImportScoped BRANCH. v1.compiler.infer_sigs lookup_resolved_sig calls lookup_resolved_sig_with_telemetry -- the sole producer of fn_parent_first_hits -- only in the else of if name_resolution_policy_is_namespace_only(), and v1.compiler.infer_env global_bare_lookup calls record_global_bare_ambiguous_silent_pick -- the sole producer of global_bare_lcp_picks and global_bare_lcp_ties -- in the matching else of the same predicate. That policy is a thread-local defaulting to TRUE whose only setters are two Rust tests, so no production compile takes the arm and all three vectors are empty by construction. ",

    "SO THE WRONG-FIELD READING WOULD HAVE PRODUCED A DECORATION: repairing the gate to ALSO read global_bare_lcp_picks and global_bare_lcp_ties -- the obvious fix, and the one this row's earlier text invites -- widens a reader over vectors that have no producer either, which is a check whose RED is unauthorable on the acceptance path, DESIGN section 4b's own question asked and answered against the repair rather than the original. ",

    "THIS CORRECTION IS READ AT SYMBOL GRAIN AND NOT EXECUTED, and that is stated rather than glossed: the two call sites, the predicate's default and its two test-only setters were read; an attempted two-arm positive control -- the same synthetic subject compiled under each policy value, counting each channel -- left all three channels at zero under BOTH arms and therefore FAILED TO DISCRIMINATE, so it is reported as a failed control and not as corroboration. ",

    "DISPOSITION TAKEN, AND IT IS A CORRECTION RATHER THAN A RUNG DROP: the gate is DELETED -- the arm in cli_run compile_emission, the CompileRun.silent_pick field no consumer read, the SilentPickSession guard, its two unit tests, and the main.rs copy with the paragraph that claimed red-on-any-raw-count as a live check. A permanently-green gate held NO RUNG, so nothing is lost and no gunbc.rung_drop row is owed; declaring one would inflate the ledger with a loss that never existed. What ends is a FALSE CLAIM OF COVERAGE. The deletion census was produced by the compiler rather than predicted: after the cut the whole workspace clippy reported exactly ONE orphan, an unused v1_rt import in main.rs, and nothing else in the tree read those two hundred and thirty lines. ",

    "THE RECORDING HOOKS THEMSELVES ARE LEFT STANDING, AND THE REASON IS AN OPERATOR DECISION WHOSE PREMISE THIS MEASUREMENT REFUTES. gunbc.ci_layer_roots resolution_divergence_silent_pick_gate_retirement_receipt (operator, 2026-08-18) deleted the surrounding census machinery and recorded PRESERVED: v1_rt silent-pick recording hooks (main.rs compile-path proxy). They are not a proxy for anything on the compile path: their producers sit behind the branch named above, so the preservation bought nothing. That makes them a SECOND artifact citable as observability while unable to observe -- this row's own class, one level out -- rather than harmless dead code. ",

    "AND THE DELETION LEAVES A GAP THAT WAS ALREADY THERE, WHICH BELONGS IN THIS ROW RATHER THAN BESIDE IT: THIS CLASS HAS NO INSTRUMENT THAT ANSWERS WHICH DECLARATION AN OCCURRENCE ACTUALLY BOUND TO. Every investigation of it so far has been reduced to GUESSING SHAPES and then perturbing them, and the guesses have been wrong repeatedly -- an arm-versus-product hypothesis, then an arm-versus-unit-arm hypothesis, then a named declarer guessed as the binder, each refuted by measurement rather than by reasoning. That is not three careless readers; it is what a class looks like when the only available evidence is a downstream diagnostic at an innocent site. ",

    "THE MEASUREMENT THAT MAKES THE GAP CONCRETE, handed over so nobody re-runs it (fierce-deer-825, on the minimal reproduction: origin/main plus one unimported module plus ONE import line, 23 blocking errors): renaming the bare UNIT arm Observed to ObservedPhaseCount in gunbc.self_host_compile_phase_frontier -- the declarer guessed to be the binder -- left roadmap_belt_actuate's occurrence REFUSING UNCHANGED, so that declarer is not the binder. THE RESULT IS CONFOUNDED AND IS RECORDED AS SUCH: the rename moved the count 23 to 29, adding six errors, three of them in that arm's own consumers, so it establishes that the roadmap occurrence SURVIVES this perturbation and NOT that the declarer is irrelevant. A rename is not a clean removal. The two remaining foreign owners of a bare Observed -- gunbc.measurement_provenance and v2.compiler.self_host.promotion_admission, both arms with payloads -- have corpus consumers too, so mutating either is confounded the same way, and the isolation cannot be finished by mutation alone. ",

    "AND THE GUESSING STOPS HERE, BECAUSE THE DIAGNOSTIC STRING ALREADY ANSWERED IT AND NOBODY HAD READ THE RENDERER. v1.compiler.infer_types node_type_shape partitions by NODE STRUCTURE and not by declarer: Product(X) requires Connective Conj, Coproduct(X) requires Disj, Named(X) is a leaf whose inferred is Resolved to a NAMED non-kernel leaf carrying an ident_span, and Primitive(X) is the ELSE of that -- a leaf that is none of those. So Primitive(Observed) IS NOT A BIND TO ANY DECLARATION AT ALL. ",

    "ALL THREE FOREIGN OWNERS ARE EXCLUDED BY THAT PARTITION RATHER THAN BY MUTATION, and the third exclusion is the one a reader will otherwise re-derive by re-running the rename: gunbc.measurement_provenance and v2.compiler.self_host.promotion_admission declare arms WITH PAYLOADS, so a bind there renders Product(Observed); gunbc.self_host_compile_phase_frontier declares a UNIT arm, which IS a leaf and reaches the same branch -- but it is named, non-kernel and carries an ident_span, so a bind there renders NAMED(Observed). None of the three can render Primitive(). The one escape that would spoil the argument was checked and is closed: Observed is NOT in std.types kernel_type_set. Independently re-derived from src/v1/04_types.dag by the lane that owns the specimen rather than taken from the lane that proposed it. ",

    "SO THE PRODUCTION SPECIMEN AND THE COMMITTED FIXTURE ARE TWO DIFFERENT MECHANISMS SHARING ONE PERTURBATION AXIS AND ONE SYMPTOM, and this is the most consequential thing in this row. The fixture's diagnostic is Coproduct(PoolSpecimenShape) vs Product(PoolSpecimenSquare) -- a REAL foreign-product bind. The production specimen's is Primitive(Observed) vs Coproduct(BeltObserve) -- NOT a bind. Both flip on closure membership and both surface as an if-join mismatch at an innocent site, which is why they read as one class. A repair of the bind channel therefore does NOT touch the production specimen, and gunbc#10737 -- lookup_binding_by_name_local at the record-literal widening seam -- is measured to do exactly that: it makes the fixture green and leaves the production specimen at 23 blocking errors on the same binary. IF THIS ROW KEEPS READING AS ONE CLASS, THAT MERGE WILL BE READ AS CLOSING SOMETHING IT DOES NOT TOUCH, which is DESIGN section 4b(1) rung inflation arriving through a merge rather than through an author's claim. ",

    "THE DISPOSITION OF THE PRODUCTION SPECIMEN: IT IS NOT AN INSTANCE OF THIS CLASS, AND IT IS RECORDED HERE AS AN UNEXPLAINED NEIGHBOUR RATHER THAN AS A SECOND SPECIMEN. The lane that contributed it asked for its own contribution to be corrected once a THIRD independent reason arrived, and it has. Reason one is the renderer partition above (Primitive() is not a bind, so no declarer can be the binder). Reason two is that gunbc#10737 repairs the fixture and leaves the specimen at 23. Reason three is a corpus property this class REQUIRES and the specimen lacks: an isolated seven-geometry measurement establishes that only a foreign STANDALONE type declaration competes for a spelling -- a foreign coproduct ARM does not perturb, and does not even contribute to the ambiguity that would repair the single-competitor case (gunbc.constructor_binding_channel case9 and case10). All four owners of the spelling Observed in that tree are ARMS, verified at declaration grain rather than by spelling count: no standalone type Observed or data Observed exists anywhere in dag/ or src/v2. So this class predicts NO perturbation for that specimen, and the specimen perturbs anyway, reproducibly, on one added import. A row carrying a specimen it cannot explain will be cited as covering it, which is DESIGN section 4b(1) rung inflation by roster membership; the specimen is therefore owned by fierce-deer-825's lane to classify, and gunbc#10683 is blocked on something that currently has no class, no fixture and no owner. ",

    "THE ORPHANED SPECIMEN LEAVES BEHIND A CONSTRAINT, AND THE CONSTRAINT IS THE DURABLE OUTPUT -- recorded here rather than in the neighbour it will eventually belong to, because that row does not exist yet and this is where a reader arrives. Measured by fierce-deer-825 across its two trees, whole-corpus with no entry so the population is total on both sides: the failing module gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate is BYTE-IDENTICAL, its declarations byte-identical, its DIRECT IMPORTS byte-identical; the resolved source population is identical at 3911 and the name-census population identical at 1112; every one of the four owners of the contested spelling is present on BOTH sides at identical diagnostic counts. The only difference in the entire tree is ONE IMPORT LINE, in a module the failing module neither imports nor is imported by. And one diagnostic appears. FOUR MECHANISMS ARE EXCLUDED BY THAT LIST RATHER THAN BY THEORY, and each died on its own falsifier: the referring module own declarations, its direct imports and build_imported_variants, the per-file flat ruling in general, and closure MEMBERSHIP of the competing owners. What survives is not a population at all: every population either lane can name is constant across the two trees, so whatever moves the binding is an ORDER -- a fold sequence, an insertion order, a memo key, or which side of rc_map_merge survives a key collision. THAT LAST SENTENCE IS A SHAPE AND NOT A LEAD: it is recorded so the next lane can rule out most of the search space before building anything, and explicitly NOT so it can be inherited as a fourth hypothesis, three having already been offered and buried. ",

    "AND A SECOND LINE ON THAT CONSTRAINT, WHICH IS THE FIRST FACT ON THIS SUBJECT THAT DISCRIMINATES WITHIN A SINGLE RUN RATHER THAN BETWEEN TWO TREES. Recorded here rather than left in a CI log nobody reopens. In one heal-generated-artifacts job -- one process, one tree, one binary, seventy-two seconds apart -- gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate TYPECHECKS CLEAN as its own subject, and then the resolve of a DIFFERENT entry point fails inside it with `Primitive(Observed) vs Coproduct(BeltObserve)`. The producer is named rather than the figures transcribed: run 34131812553, job 101773452584, on gunbc#10683. THE CONSEQUENCE IS WHAT MAKES IT WORTH A LINE: every earlier statement of this specimen was CROSS-TREE and required someone to build two trees to see anything, so the search space was the diff between them. This is the same phenomenon inside ONE invocation, so the search space collapses to whatever differs between `typecheck this module` and `resolve that entry point` -- both reachable from a single command, both holding a different answer about the same bytes at the same time. That also independently corroborates the constraint above by a second route: it cannot be a property of the module or of the corpus, because neither varies here. NO MECHANISM IS ATTACHED, deliberately: four have now been proposed against this specimen and four have died, and the discipline that has actually paid on this subject is two-arm geometries that predict a differing outcome, not accounts of why. Contributed by fierce-deer-825, who owns the orphan. ",

    "WHAT REMAINS OPEN AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT GUESSED: Primitive() also covers a leaf that WAS resolved but to something structurally empty -- no ident_span, or an authored name of None -- so the established claim is NEGATIVE (not a product or coproduct bind) and does not yet separate never-resolved from resolved-to-empty. ",

    "WHY THE OBSERVABILITY GAP AND THE DELETED GATE ARE ONE SUBJECT AND NOT TWO. The data that would answer the question EXISTS in the shape the recorders already carry -- global_bare_lcp_pick carries env_module_path, name, candidate_count and CHOSEN_MODULE_PATH, which is exactly which-declaration-did-this-bind-to -- and it is unreachable for the same reason the gate was permanently green: its producer sits in the ImportScoped else. So the gap is not repaired by building a new instrument, and it was never repaired by the gate either: a gate refusing on a COUNT never answers WHICH, so even an armed gate would not have told anyone what they needed. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER FOR THE OBSERVABILITY GAP, named as a capability and deliberately separate from this class's own next-rung trigger -- and it carries TWO independent questions rather than one, which is what should make it rank: which declaration an occurrence bound to, and whether a Primitive() rendering means never-resolved or resolved-to-empty. Both are blocked on the same absent capability: the chosen-candidate payload recorded on the SHIPPED namespace-only arm -- or at the occurrence-binding seam -- rather than only on the dead legacy one, so that an ordinary compile can be asked which declaration an occurrence bound to. That is a producer change and not a gate, and it is not taken in this change: it is a resolver-path edit whose scope is the namespace cut's, and shipping it beside a deletion would fuse a measurement capability into a hygiene cut. ",

    "SO THE DISPOSITION THE REFUTATION IMPLIES IS TO DELETE THE HOOKS TOO, AND IT IS DELIBERATELY NOT TAKEN HERE. Deleting them touches 6 .dag authorities (04_env, 04_sigs, 04_method, runtime_rust, extdeps.languages.rust.emit, std.primitives), three separate builtin and bridge rosters keyed on the same four names, and a --required-regen including the bootstrap edge v1.compiler.runtime_rust to v1_rt.rs run twice because the seed carries its own emitter's string -- about 640 lines for dead code on a dead branch. That is a cost-versus-benefit call and NOT a judgement that the hooks are fine, and overturning an operator-signed preservation is the operator's decision rather than this change's. The natural motion is to delete them WITH the ImportScoped arm itself when the namespace cut retires it, which is one cut instead of a bootstrap regen now. ",

    "Section 4b asks whether a check's RED is AUTHORABLE before the check is written; here it is not, and nobody asked. ",

    "Fixing one axis would leave it looking fixed. ",

    "The gate HAD to be REPAIRED OR DELETED, and if repaired its RED had to be DEMONSTRATED rather than assumed. THAT IS SETTLED AND THE DISPOSITION IS RECORDED ABOVE: it was DELETED, as a correction rather than a rung drop, because every one of its three producers sits behind the dead ImportScoped arm, so repairing it to read the other vectors would have been a decoration. The sentence is kept in the past tense rather than removed, because it is the obligation the disposition discharged and a reader who finds only the answer cannot tell what question was asked -- but it must not stand in the present tense, or it sends a later lane to repair work already ruled out. ",

    "Whether the type channel bypasses global_bare_lookup or reaches it past the policy branch was NOT isolated when that sentence was written, and is now ANSWERED for the production specimen by the renderer partition recorded above rather than by a guess: Primitive() is not a bind to any declaration, so no channel reaching any of the three foreign declarers can account for it. What remains open is the narrower question the receipt below names -- whether Primitive() means never-resolved or resolved-to-empty -- and that is stated there rather than here. ",

    "INDEPENDENT CORROBORATION, from the lane that hit this first and reached it from the other side, and cited as gunbc#10210 -- the PR, whose diff survives squash-merge and branch deletion, rather than the branch commits, which do not: a four-arm table over the real specimen in which the decisive row holds the branch RESTRUCTURE constant and changes only the NAMES -- renaming the two arms to unique spellings, with the if-expression untouched, is GREEN. ",

    "Its mirror row is restructured, green, and STILL FORKED, which is why a green there proves nothing about the fork. ",

    "That is an ORTHOGONAL PERTURBATION AXIS rather than a second opinion: every probe in this row varies POOL MEMBERSHIP with the spelling held constant, and that table varies the SPELLING with pool membership held constant, so neither alone excludes the other's confound and together they do. ",

    "It isolates the collision as the cause rather than the branch shape, and it carries the harm in one sentence: the compiler sent an author to restructure an innocent if-join for two hours and the shipped commit message records the disagreement as undiagnosed. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder on the source-to-interpretation path, because the wrong binding is taken silently and the only refusal is a downstream consequence at an innocent site. ",

    "Under DESIGN section 4b(1) the class's rung is the MINIMUM across in-scope paths, and byte-identical source accepting at one closure grain and refusing at another means neither grain establishes anything. ",

    "CEILING, WITH ITS REASON: structurally guaranteed, not structurally impossible. ",

    "Nothing stops two modules from spelling a type the same, so the invalid state stays WRITABLE; what is attainable is that no Accepted program RESOLVES THROUGH one, which is a refusal derived from modeled structure and therefore rung 3. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as the capability: a declaration-identity authority that decides a reference's binder from the referencing module's own containment chain for EVERY occurrence channel -- types, coproduct arms, record-literal heads and free calls alike -- sufficient to refuse an off-chain or multiply-on-chain reference at resolve time rather than adjudicate it. ",

    "That is the same capability gunbc.recurring_failure_mode empty_observation_narrow already names from the census direction -- one namespace census over the one Node tree, not a second check beside the type-name one -- and reaching rung 4 additionally needs the second declaration to be unwritable, which is a further, separate capability. ",

    "**THE VALUE CHANNEL, MEASURED 2026-09-07 BY calm-ferret-398, AND IT IS A DIFFERENT MECHANISM FROM EVERY PROBE ABOVE.** Every specimen in this row until now varies pool membership at a TYPE or coproduct-arm occurrence. ",

    "The occurrence channel this row's own next-rung trigger names last -- free calls -- had never been probed, and it does not behave the way the type channel does. ",

    "THE SPECIMEN THAT STARTED IT: src/v2/lens/grounding.dag calls layer_prefix_from_dotted_qualified_name, declared in v2.std.cross_tree.resolution, as a bare name with no import; the module carries three import lines and calls a number of functions it does not import, and it is accepted under one required run and refused under another over identical bytes; the calls are enumerated by the refusal itself -- gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/lens/grounding.dag emits one function not found in scope per unimported callee, so the population at that site is re-derivable rather than transcribed. ",

    "THE FIRST FINDING IS AN ABSENCE, and it is larger than the specimen: THE VALUE CHANNEL HAS NO DIAGNOSTIC AT ALL. ",

    "The mask check that emits the UnlistedImportUse advisory lives in the TYPE resolver -- v1.compiler.infer_resolve resolve_node, keyed on type_name -- so a bare cross-module CALL produces neither a refusal nor an advisory, and the emitter then synthesises the use-line the author never wrote. ",

    "That is not thin coverage, it is DESIGN section 5's fabricated-plausible-output arm: the compiler invents the dependency that makes the program work and says nothing. ",

    "The type channel additionally has a whole-tree census (v1.compiler.cli_run compile_clean_diagnostic_census, whose unlisted_import_rows carry this class); the value channel had neither a census nor a diagnostic. ",

    "THE MECHANISM, EXECUTED RATHER THAN READ, and it is sharper than pool membership as this row has stated it so far: A MODULE WITH ZERO IMPORT LINES HAS ITS CROSS-MODULE DEPENDENCIES MANUFACTURED FROM ITS BARE REFERENCES, AND A MODULE WITH AT LEAST ONE IMPORT LINE DOES NOT. ",

    "v1.compiler.cli_run ModuleGraphFactsLive reference_only_direct_import_paths derives reference edges as selection_adjacency minus adjacency and the two agree on an import-bearing file, so the compiler follows a bare call to its definer for the first and never for the second. ",

    "So the binding of a bare call is not decided by the call, by the definer, or by the entry's imports: it is decided by whether the REFERENCING module happens to carry an import line naming something else entirely, and after that by whether some unrelated module in the entry's closure happens to import the definer. ",

    "COMMITTED DISCRIMINATING FIXTURE, beside if_join_pool_binding and in its idiom -- fixtures.free_call_pool_binding, with the perturbation reduced to ONE LINE. ",

    "ARM A, ACCEPTED: subject_module imports nothing and calls definer_module's pool_specimen_free_call; the closure comes back with three sources although no file in it names definer_module in an import line, and the compile reports 0 diagnostics. ",

    "ARM B, REFUSED: subject_with_import is the same call with one import of unrelated_module -- a module that neither declares nor mentions the call or its definer -- and the same command refuses with function pool_specimen_free_call not found in scope. ",

    "ARM C, ACCEPTED, excluding the containment confound: subject_offchain calls a definer under a DIFFERENT top-level container, sharing no ancestor below the root, and resolves identically, so ancestor-chain distance is not the variable and the import line is. ",

    "Reproduce all three with gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root fixtures/free_call_pool_binding --source-root fixtures/free_call_pool_binding_offchain --entry fixtures/free_call_pool_binding/closure_without_definer.dag, and the same at closure_with_import.dag and closure_offchain.dag. ",

    "The fixture is outside the compiled source roots for the same reason if_join_pool_binding is: an authentic specimen committed into dag or src/v2 would be a real corpus fork. ",

    "THE THREE ARMS ARE REPRODUCED BY COMMAND AND EXECUTED BY NOTHING ENROLLED, WHICH IS RECORDED RATHER THAN GLOSSED because a fixture cited as coverage is worse than an absent one. ",

    "The harness that would run them is missing and its absence is MEASURED, not assumed: gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census compile_dag_diagnostic_census -- the corpus's one nested-compile surface -- resolves only a probe source's AUTHORED import closure, so a bare call to a corpus function from an import-less probe refuses there with InternalError function:<name>, confirmed on two definers in two different source roots. ",

    "The ACCEPTING arm is therefore unauthorable in it, and the one instrument available is blind to exactly the manufactured edge this class is about -- the same asymmetry one level up, in the thing that would measure it. ",

    "Under DESIGN section 4b that missing harness is this channel's next-rung trigger and not a ceiling: a nested compile deriving its closure the way the production one does would run all three arms unchanged, and if_join_pool_binding stands the same way for the same reason. ",

    "THE POPULATION, WITH ITS PRODUCER NAMED RATHER THAN ITS NUMBERS TRANSCRIBED: v2.lens.manufactured_dependency_census, run as gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/lens/manufactured_dependency_census.dag --function main, folds the difference between the two edge producers v2.lens.module_graph already owns -- it adds no third producer, which that module's dependency_edge_source_migration_note forbids -- and its tally reports authored import edges, reference-derived edges, manufactured edges and the modules carrying them. ",

    "Its main is a gate rather than a report: it refuses on an empty import set, on an empty reference set, and on a zero difference, so a producer that stopped deriving cannot be read as a corpus with nothing to find. ",

    "ONE MEASURED FACT THE LENS ESTABLISHES THAT WAS PREVIOUSLY ASSUMED: the two edge sets are already DISJOINT on this corpus -- every reference-derived edge is manufactured, none coincides with an authored import -- so the subtraction is currently the identity. ",

    "It is kept because nothing guarantees that: the host union deduplicates reference-first on exact identity, which is only necessary if overlap is possible. ",

    "THE FIGURE IS A LOWER BOUND AND MUST BE QUOTED AS ONE, which is the denominator error this class invites. ",

    "The lens can only see modules whose edges are manufactured, that is import-LESS ones; the bare cross-module calls of import-BEARING modules -- the specimen's own among them -- produce no edge, no advisory and no row, so they are invisible to it BY CONSTRUCTION rather than measured at zero. ",

    "That invisible half is not quoted here as a figure, because no committed producer derives it: the only instrument that reached it was a static scan with no entry point, and a number without one is the transcription this row already refuses elsewhere. Its existence is established by the specimen and its size is an open measurement, which is itself part of what the capability owes. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT, on this channel: below the ladder, and for a strictly worse reason than the type channel's. ",

    "There the wrong binding is taken silently and a downstream refusal at least fires at an innocent site; here the MISSING binding is manufactured silently and the program is accepted, so on the arm that matters most there is no refusal anywhere. ",

    "CEILING AND TRIGGER ARE THIS ROW'S EXISTING ONES AND ARE NOT RESTATED, with one obligation added to the trigger's sufficiency rather than to its name: the capability is not sufficient while it can be demonstrated on the type channel alone. ",

    "Its acceptance must include the value channel -- arm B of the fixture above must keep refusing, arm A must JOIN it in refusing rather than continuing to resolve, and a value-channel census must exist for the import-bearing population, because a rule that binds free calls without one is unfalsifiable over exactly the modules this specimen came from. ",

    "WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: no repair is attempted here and none should be read into it. ",

    "The resolution rule is the namespace cut's subject; this is its measurement, and the ordering between them is unchanged.",

    "**THE EVALUATION CHANNEL, MEASURED 2026-09-11 BY stern-bear-703, AND IT FALSIFIES THE INVARIANT MORE STRONGLY THAN ANY PROBE ABOVE.** Every specimen in this row flips on CLOSURE COMPOSITION and is deterministic given a closure. This one flips on NOTHING OBSERVABLE: identical files, identical binary, identical command, and the verdict differs from run to run. ",

    "It is a different layer from the type and value channels above: the typechecker accepts the program every time, and the wrong binding is taken by the TREE-WALKING INTERPRETER at evaluation. ",

    "THE SPECIMEN THAT FOUND IT: gunbc-private's one-process witness roster, test.claim.private_roster_witness, failed with TypeError cannot access field 'field' on Fn in 3 of 4 local runs of one unchanged tree once a witness importing the public roadmap stack joined it, while every member witness passed alone. The data/fn homonym in main's own closure is gigabyte: data in extdeps.vendor.gigabyte, fn in std.measure. ",

    "THE MECHANISM, READ IN THE SOURCE: v1_interpreter.rs InterpContext::build_scope_indexes_with_module_order projects graph.item_registry -- an im::HashMap keyed by declaration identity, hashed with std RandomState and therefore seeded per process -- into bare_item_registry by re-keying every entry to its BARE name, with collect() keeping the last write. Iteration order decides which declarer's ItemInfo survives a homonym, and that order changes every process. The comment above it says the projection reproduces the map this field used to receive; that stopped being true when the source became identity-keyed, because the re-key is where the randomness now enters. ",

    "THE CHECK EXISTS AND ONE CONSUMER DOES NOT READ IT, which is the finding rather than the missing sort. The same function counts bare spellings into bare_name_counts and derives ambiguous_bare_function_names, and lookup_fn_from consults that set: for an ambiguous name it resolves the NODE through the referring file's own module, then its explicit import, before the shared slot. The variable slow path in eval then takes the item's KIND -- DataItem versus FnItem -- from bare_item_registry, which never consults the ambiguous set. So for an ambiguous name the node is chosen by locality and the kind by hash order, and when an FnItem wins over a data reference the interpreter returns Value::Fn wrapping the data declaration; the next field access raises exactly the TypeError above. ",

    "COMMITTED DISCRIMINATING FIXTURE, in this row's idiom and outside the compiled source roots: fixtures.data_fn_homonym_evaluation. data_declarer declares a record-valued data and reads its field inside its own module; fn_declarer declares a fn with the same bare spelling and nothing else; closure_with_both imports both, closure_without_fn is the same subject without fn_declarer. ",

    "Reproduce with gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root fixtures/data_fn_homonym_evaluation --entry fixtures/data_fn_homonym_evaluation/closure_with_both.dag --function evaluation_main, repeated. Measured with one binary (sha256 prefix 33f179b2da723442, built from seed commit 1c0c30d416 -- not the CI build, which is why the rate is quoted as observed rather than as the class's): closure_with_both failed with the TypeError in 1 of 12 runs from this tree and in 7 of 12 when the same three modules sat in a larger overlay closure; closure_without_fn passed 6 of 6. The rate moves with the closure because the hash layout does; the flip does not need the closure to move at all. THE CI BUILD REPRODUCES IT TOO, so this is not an artifact of the local seed: gunbc-private actions run 34607828252, whose gunbc was built from the pinned public revision 0ab33d7a, failed its one-process roster on head fc18b2a with TypeError { msg: \"cannot access field 'field' on Fn\" } on the tree that first showed it; the control is gunbc-private actions run 34609121190 on head 54535de, the same composition with only the importing witness moved to its own process, which passed. These rates are an incident datum on a named non-CI binary, not an instrument reading: when the repeated-run witness below exists they dissolve into its output and are deleted here, never updated by hand. ",

    "THE REPAIR IS TWO LAYERS, AND THE FIRST IS NOT A SETTLE-FOR-DETERMINISTIC. The slow path reads ONE fact -- what this name denotes -- from TWO lookups: the node from the file-aware lookup_fn_from and the kind from a hash-order bare winner. That is a single-authority fork under DESIGN section 3, and the nondeterminism is its symptom, not the defect. LAYER 1 collapses both reads onto the one resolved node; that is the section 3 repair, and determinism falls out of it. LAYER 2 is the class climb on top of a fixed defect: an ambiguous bare name that still reaches the shared slot refuses as a typed ambiguous reference, namespace-resolution-design section 13's ancestor-chain uniqueness applied to this channel, landing with a homonym census and the renames it forces in the same change -- never a refusal with an allow-list. This fixture is the discriminating red layer 1 cites; neither layer is attempted here. ",


    "THE FIXTURE IS REPRODUCED BY COMMAND AND EXECUTED BY NOTHING ENROLLED, recorded rather than glossed as with free_call_pool_binding above: a single run proves nothing about a nondeterministic defect, and the enrolment that fits it is a repeated-run witness on the pinned build, which does not exist yet. ",

    "CONSEQUENCE FOR CI TRIAGE, stated because it changes how reds are read: a per-process seed can change how a reference EVALUATES, so a nondeterministic red on an unchanged tree is not evidence of infrastructure flakiness until this channel is ruled out for that closure. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT, on this channel: below the ladder, because the wrong declaration is evaluated silently and the only symptom is a downstream TypeError at a site that is correct. CEILING ON THIS CHANNEL: structurally guaranteed, reachable -- a wall after grounding, not a ratchet. Layer 1 has a lane (gunbc#11065: the evaluator now takes the kind from the resolved node). Layer 2 is the declared frontier recorded in the four receipts below, whose population is measured by an existing producer and whose authority is claim_scope_for's out-of-region set, NOT ambiguous_bare_function_names. ",


    "LAYER 2 IS A DECLARED FRONTIER, PARKED, AND ITS POPULATION IS MEASURED BY AN EXISTING PRODUCER (contributed by calm-bear-43 from the layer-1 work in gunbc#11065). cli_run claim_scope_for marks, per claim scope, a bare name claimed twice with both claims outside the author's import region, so nothing the author wrote ranks them and the shared slot decides. required_floor_runner prints the aggregate as [floor-bare-name-ambiguity]. Main run 34571176215 at ec1571e8: scopes_affected=332 of 676, names_total=25143 (SUMMED over scopes, not distinct), worst_scope=114. The producer prints counts, not names, so the distinct count and the list are not yet known; at that size a refusal is a rename programme, not a repair. ",

    "THE CONCEPT HAS TWO PRODUCERS THAT DISAGREE, WHICH IS ITSELF A SECTION 3 FORK. v1_interpreter build_scope_indexes_with_module_order derives ambiguous_bare_function_names from bare_name_counts, which counts every top-level declaration of every kind (the function in its name is wrong about its own population), including collisions inside the authored region that precedence legitimately settles; lookup_fn_from gates its file-aware tiers on it. cli_run claim_scope_for's ambiguous set counts only out-of-region collisions. The refusal's authority MUST be claim_scope_for's population, because authored-region shadowing is sanctioned, not ambiguous; the other set is re-derived from it or retired IN THE SAME CHANGE AS THE WALL, never consulted beside it. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, THE CAPABILITY: a distinct-name list of out-of-region bare-name collisions per claim scope, emitted by claim_scope_for into the floor receipt. The count alone does not satisfy it: 114 in one scope could be 114 distinct names or a few repeated, and only the distinct list sizes the renames that must land with the wall. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Membership is decidable and grounded -- the authored region and the reaching modules are both facts the scope already carries -- so this is a wall after grounding, NOT a ratchet, and the refusal lands together with its renames and never with an allow-list. ",

    "THERE IS NO WHOLE-CORPUS REGISTRY, established by trying, so the next author does not repeat the walk. Walking every corpus module through the evaluator's own fragment derivation, in batches of closures importing unrelated modules, refuses at COMPILE on cross-module variant collisions, e.g. StandingSatisfied appearing in both StandingVerdict and FabricCellAddressStanding, before any scope index is built. Registries exist only per closure, per gunbc run entry and per floor claim scope, so the per-claim-scope census is the RIGHT population by construction, not a convenient proxy for a corpus-wide one. ",

    "CROSS-LINK: this class is what makes join_judged_against_its_sibling_rather_than_its_declared_context visible; repairing that join alone would silence the diagnostic while leaving the wrong binding in place, so the ordering is resolution first.",
